    <briefdescription>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>File format of an ELF Segment header.</para><para>Byte order of members depends on e_ident value in file header. This code comes directly from &quot;Executable and
Linkable Format (ELF)&quot;, Portable Formats Specification, Version 1.1, Tool Interface Standards (TIS) and not from any header file. The 64-bit structure is gleaned from the Linux elf(5) man page. Segment table entries (a.k.a., ELF program headers) either describe process segments or give supplementary info which does not contribute to the process image. </para>    </detaileddescription>
